.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored `ledger/` also
# matches `src/cost_autopilot/ledger/`, which would silently leave the ledger
# source package out of every commit.
/ledger/
# Anchored for the same reason as /ledger/: unanchored, `validate/` would also
# match `src/cost_autopilot/validate/` and leave stage 03's source uncommitted.
# `shadow/` holds request text and answers; it must never be committed.
/shadow/
/validate/
# Stage 04's runtime output directory, anchored for the same reason as the three
# above: unanchored, `report/` would also match `src/cost_autopilot/report/` and
# leave stage 04's source uncommitted. A rendered month is derived data — it can
# be regenerated from the ledger and the verdicts at any time. The copies worth
# keeping are the ones under `docs/examples/`, which ARE committed and which
# carry a banner saying whether they came from a live run or a dry one.
/report/
# Everything `autopilot.demo.toml` writes: the quota-fit live demo's own ledger,
# shadow file, verdicts and report. Separate from the four above so a demo run
# can never be mistaken for, or overwrite, a real month.
/demo/
/runs/
# The temporary file `apply-proposal` writes and then renames over
# autopilot.toml. It should never survive a successful or a failed run; it is
# listed so a crash mid-apply cannot leave a half-edited config staged.
*.toml.proposed
.DS_Store
.coverage
